   "text": "The pattern fits two phases: a near-cubic spinel and a tetragonally distorted spinel.\n\n**Peak positions**\n- About 18.4\u00b0 (I \u2248 80).\n- A broad hump near 29.3\u00b0 (\u2248 25).\n- About 34.15\u00b0 (\u2248 46).\n- About 34.95\u00b0 (\u2248 43).\n- About 35.75\u00b0 (100).\n- About 37.3\u00b0 (\u2248 27).\n- About 43.45\u00b0 (\u2248 83).\n\n**Phase 1: cubic spinel, mp-772177 (Li2Fe3CuO8)**\n- The peaks at 18.4\u00b0, 35.75\u00b0 and 43.45\u00b0 have d-spacings in the ratios of spinel (111), (311) and (400), for a \u2248 8.33 \u00c5.\n- Li2Fe3CuO8 is a nearly cubic spinel with a cubic-equivalent a \u2248 8.39\u20138.41 \u00c5. That predicts (111) \u2248 18.3\u00b0, (311) \u2248 35.5\u00b0 and (400) \u2248 43.1\u00b0.\n- The observed peaks sit 0.1\u20130.35\u00b0 higher, a lattice about 0.8% smaller than the CIF. I am assuming the simulation applied a lattice strain; this is the main weakness of the assignment.\n- Li sits on the tetrahedral sites, so the (220) reflection near 30.3\u00b0 should be very weak, and none is seen.\n\n**Phase 2: distorted spinel, mp-33631 (TiZn2O4)**\n- Converting its primitive cell gives an orthorhombic cell of about 5.97 \u00d7 6.02 \u00d7 8.74 \u00c5.\n- This predicts (112) \u2248 29.3\u00b0, (013)/(103) \u2248 34.2\u00b0 and (121)/(211) \u2248 34.9\u00b0. These match the 29.3\u00b0 hump and the 34.15\u00b0/34.95\u00b0 doublet.\n\n**Candidates rejected**\n- **Sr2YRuO6:** its strongest reflection would be near 30.5\u00b0, which is absent.\n- **Mg3ZnO4:** its rock-salt peaks would fall near 36.3\u00b0 and 42.2\u00b0, which do not match.\n- **LiCuSbO4:** its strong c-axis elongation predicts peaks near 17.5\u00b0 and 18.0\u00b0, not 18.4\u00b0.\n- **Others:** the perovskite and brownmillerite candidates put their strongest lines near 26.5\u201333.8\u00b0, which do not match.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-772177\", \"mp-33631\"], \"confidence\": 0.65, \"note\": \"Cubic-spinel lines at 18.4, 35.75 and 43.45 deg fit Li2Fe3CuO8 (lattice about 0.8% smaller than the CIF), and the 29.3, 34.15 and 34.95 deg peaks fit the tetragonally distorted TiZn2O4 spinel.\"}",
